In article <3373f3e5.88920405@news>, 
weinzerl@xpoint.at (wi) writes:

> I've got a MicroVax 3300 which needs a DSSI-Drive to boot. 
> ...
> Or even better, tell me how to boot of a NON-DSSI-Drive

This is no problem.   I have been booting from a non-DSSI disk
on a 3300 for the last two years.   We have a Q-Bus SCSI controller
(Andromeda Systems SCDC) with two 2.3GB Seagate drives and an
Archive Python DAT drive.   To boot, simply type "BOOT DUA0" at
the ">>>" prompt.   You can also set it as the default boot device
by typing "SET BOOT DUA0".   It is not restricted to unit zero, either.
We boot from DUA5 (the Andromeda controller lets us partition
the drives).

