>The problem is that the KDA50 won't attach to a device driver but will show up 
>as a used address with no interrupt vector in the SHOW QBUS console command

I think you want to set the KDA50 to 760340:

$ mcr sysgen
SYSGEN>  CONFIG
DEVICE> kda50 4
%SYSGEN-I-EQV_NOTICE, equivalent name - device KDA50 will be output as UDA
DEVICE> tk50 1
%SYSGEN-I-EQV_NOTICE, equivalent name - device TK50 will be output as TU81
DEVICE> tsv05 1
%SYSGEN-I-EQV_NOTICE, equivalent name - device TSV05 will be output as TS11
DEVICE>  Exit
Device: TS11    Name: MSA        CSR: 772520     Vector: 224    Support: yes
Device: UDA     Name: PUA        CSR: 772150     Vector: 154    Support: yes
Device: TU81    Name: PTA        CSR: 774500     Vector: 260    Support: yes
Device: UDA     Name: PUB        CSR: 760334*    Vector: 300*   Support: yes
Device: UDA     Name: PUC        CSR: 760340*    Vector: 304*   Support: yes
Device: UDA     Name: PUD        CSR: 760344*    Vector: 310*   Support: yes

